  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Raytheon has $8.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Raytheon won 405 awards so far in the fiscal year for an average award size of $21.3M, and obligations are down 19.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $5.9B in FY21 to $10.7B in FY25 before reaching $8.6B in FY26. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest market for Raytheon at $6.4B in FY2026 to date, followed by Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $998M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $824M. Smaller markets include Engineering Services at $160M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Propulsion Unit and Propulsion Unit Parts Manufacturing at $123M. The current-year totals are partial, and the listed award values and expiring-contract entries are total contract values when those tables are present.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Raytheon's obligations by market?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the dominant market with $6.4B in obligations. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing and R&D (Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences) are the next largest markets at $998M and $824M respectively. The remaining top markets range from $160M to $2.8M, showing a steep drop after the top three."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have Raytheon's obligations changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations increased from $5.9B in FY21 to $10.7B in FY25, then moved to $8.6B in FY26. The current-year total is partial and obligations are down 19.5% year over year compared with the prior year."
      }
    ]
  },
